{"chunk_id": "fc90fc0bbab7", "text": "Vasishtha\u2019s divine cow Shabala defends her master against King Vishwamitra. Declaring that the spiritual power of a sage surpasses the might of a warrior, she asks permission to destroy the king\u2019s pride. At Vasishtha\u2019s command she miraculously generates armies\u2014foreign soldiers and strange golden\u2011skinned warriors\u2014who overwhelm Vishwamitra\u2019s forces. Even when Vishwamitra counters with powerful weapons, Shabala produces more warriors from her own body, annihilating the king\u2019s elephants, chariots, and troops. Vishwamitra\u2019s hundred sons attack Vasishtha but are instantly burned to ashes when the sage utters a single sacred sound. Humiliated and stripped of glory, Vishwamitra abandons his kingdom and turns to severe asceticism. Winning the favor of Shiva, he gains divine knowledge and celestial weapons, setting the stage for a renewed confrontation with Vasishtha and marking the beginning of his transformation from king to spiritual seeker.\nShabala magically creates armies that destroy Vishwamitra\u2019s forces; his sons die, and the humiliated king turns to severe penance and seeks divine weapons from Shiva.\nThemes: spiritual power vs royal power, divine manifestations, humiliation and transformation, asceticism and penance, divine weapons", "vector": [0.0007705740863457322, -0.020130932331085205, 0.004604917019605637, 0.012221389450132847, -0.026868192479014397, 0.015468748286366463, -0.02657175250351429, -0.02905106358230114, -0.011716094799339771, -0.027232004329562187, 0.007714162580668926, 0.015616968274116516, 0.008616955019533634, 0.010516862384974957, 0.005349384155124426, 0.023337867110967636, 0.05794043466448784, -0.004076042212545872, 0.027892256155610085, 0.004874407313764095, 0.010516862384974957, -0.0011352283181622624, 0.011796941980719566, 0.020211778581142426, -0.02364778146147728, 0.010638133622705936, 0.019066445529460907, -0.0218556709587574, -0.002169397659599781, -0